Z||000007||Voyd||04-02-2000||05:23 AM||||hahaha same here. the roof and decklid are faded badly but the sides and hood are like new.||||reg||1
Z||000008||RFMike||04-02-2000||09:28 AM||||With only 60K on the motor, it would probably  be worth it to repaint it.  <BR>My 86 GT was repainted by the original owner, and it looks like it just rolled off the lot.  No, I didn't get it for the Pez dispenser (good one, Vaana), but the money I paid was worth it to me.  Every time I wash and wax it, I feel just like I did when I was 18, with my first car.  Amazing.<P>If you have the cash for paint, do it.  You'll be glad you did.<P>Good luck,<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000009||phillip||04-02-2000||11:00 AM|||| mine is about 4 different colors from playing with body panels with possibly more to come. i still get ocassional compliments on the car. don't know when i'll get done but i have no problem driving it as is. they're just neat cars.||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||04-02-2000||11:07 AM||||I just got my Coupe painted !!! It cost me $1200.00 out the door. The guy paints out of his own little, one car, garage/shack...lol<BR>The car came out great !!! Maybe not showcar quality but close. So start saving your money...like I did. And find someone to do a "backyard paint job". Talk to the local HOTRODDERS they'll know who to get ahold of. Or you can bring it to OHIO and I'll set you up with my guy !!!||||reg||3
Z||000011||lowCG||04-02-2000||01:30 PM||||It was hard to spend $1500 on a new motor that still needs modification$ to go into the car,when the car itself still needs paint,fender put on,door hinges.<BR>So the other day,I rebuilt the steering column that was flopping around all over,and I feel alot better about my old car now.I also took the big,ugly,stock shift knob off and carefully ground it down to more of a ball shape,looks great,cost less!||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||04-02-2000||06:27 PM||||You haven't seen mine. Paint chips. Keyed. fried clear coat that's fairly hidden.<P>Interior not to bad. Even have the optional floor mats. one small tear in drivers seat.<P>4 cyl runs like a scalded bat. Not bad at all for nearly 150,000 miles.<P>Don't assume we all have show cars.||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||04-02-2000||10:07 PM||||Maybe some of these guys have Fieros bought with Pokemon cards, and some of em have show quality rides. I can pretty much guarantee they aren't the same guys!<BR>My GT has a 50' paint job, ripped up drivers seat, some jacked up cracked up sail panels... and a brand spankin new motor!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Someday I wll have that pretty paint job (leaning away from yellow to a lexus-like light gold) but in the meantime, my cash is better invested in making it liveable inside the car and longlasting. Don't despair cuz it isn't ready for the show circuit. Just drive the hell out of it and clean clean clean.||||reg||1
